Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||05-12-2001||09:36 PM||||hmmmm, I had this happen to me for a wile too...what I did was take out the temp/fuel guages and cleaned off the two metal prongs cuz they were rusted..I just used some sand paper.  Good Luck<BR><P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||10
Z||000002||sjp777||05-12-2001||09:41 PM||||I seem to remember something about 86 temp gauges being wired wrong from the factory. Anybody else remember anything about this?<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||05-12-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sjp777:<BR><B>I seem to remember something about 86 temp gauges being wired wrong from the factory. Anybody else remember anything about this?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your memory is sort of correct ... <B>ALL</B> Fieros had their coolant temperature gauges wired incorrectly at the factory.<P>See  <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A>  for rewiring instructions.<P>Paul||||reg||1
